&=& \left( \frac{x}{b} \right)^{\frac{1}{2} - \mu_0} \cdot
\frac{K_\nu\left[ \sqrt{2} \frac{x^{1-\theta}}{1-\theta}  \sqrt{\alpha}\right]}{K_\nu\left[ \sqrt{2} \frac{b^{1-\theta}}{1-\theta}  \sqrt{\alpha}\right]} \tag{1}
\end{eqnarray}
Note that the quantity in $(1)$ is a valid Laplace transform.
Indeed we know from here that for small values of $ z $ the modified Bessel function of the second kind behaves as $ K_\nu(z) \simeq z^{-\nu} $ for $ \nu > 0 $. As such it is clearly seen that $ \lim_{\alpha \rightarrow 0} u_\alpha^{(b)}(x) = 1 $ as it should be.
